-Revision 94 implements `NEIGHBOR1` on top of the `PARCORE1` scheduler. FEAS1 now compresses each exact cKDTree witness block into canonical witness-oriented CSR while performing its unchanged support/capacity reduction, persists that forward graph as a reconstructible authenticated execution cache, and releases ragged neighbor objects immediately after canonical reduction. MVIDX1 adopts the authenticated forward CSR and therefore performs no second geometric sweep on a cache hit; a missing or stale cache is rebuilt once through the same global exact engine. The existing MVIDX CSR-to-CSC inversion remains unchanged and is the subject of the next `MVIDX-REUSE1` gate. Scientific FEAS1/MVIDX authorities, TARGET-DATA2 selection semantics, training/evaluation semantics, and GPU authority are unchanged. The active qualification checkpoint remains MACE-MPA-0 medium, while NEIGHBOR1 contains no foundation-specific assumptions and remains valid for MACE-MH-1 campaigns. GPU performance authority remains deferred.
+Revision 95 completes `MVIDX-REUSE1` on top of `NEIGHBOR1` and `PARCORE1`. On an authenticated NEIGHBOR1 cache hit, MVIDX1 now performs no geometry and schedules independent required-family inversions plus hard-obligation inversion through one bounded deterministic work queue. Each individual CSR-to-CSC conversion remains a deterministic compiled counting transpose with one native execution lane; canonical family order is restored after arbitrary task completion. The former per-row sorted/unique validator is replaced by an exact vectorized CSR-boundary-masked predicate, removing the dominant Python-loop overhead. Scientific FEAS1/MVIDX authorities, TARGET-DATA2 selection semantics, training/evaluation semantics, and GPU authority are unchanged. The active qualification checkpoint remains MACE-MPA-0 medium, while the optimization contains no foundation-specific assumptions and remains valid for MACE-MH-1 campaigns. `COVREF-PAR1` is next; GPU performance authority remains deferred.
